{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-sym2-adjoint-traceless-spin-two","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:sym2-adjoint-traceless-spin-two","kind":"proposition","title":"The traceless part of $\\mathrm{Sym}^2(V_1)$ is the spin-$2$ object $V_2$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-su2-emergence","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-spin-labels","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-spin-labels-su2","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-ew-triplet-charge-spin-from-involution"],"cites":["references/fulton-harris1991"],"tags":["spin","gauge-group","symmetric-square","clebsch-gordan"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2AdjointSpinTwo.adjoint_sym2_traceless_is_spin_two","text":"sym2-adjoint-traceless-spin-two.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:sym2-adjoint-traceless-spin-two\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G = \\mathrm{Aut}^{\\otimes}(\\tau) \\cong \\mathrm{SU}(2)</code> be the gauge group of <a href=\"#thm:su2-emergence\" data-at=\"quantum-observable-universes/emergence/emergence-volume-rigidity\">the emergence theorem</a>, with simple objects <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_j</code> labelled by <a href=\"#prop:spin-labels\" data-at=\"quantum-observable-universes/emergence/emergence-spin-labels\">spin</a> and adjoint <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_1 \\cong \\mathrm{Ad}(A)</code>. Then</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathrm{Sym}^2(V_1) \\;\\cong\\; V_0 \\oplus V_2,\n  \\qquad\n  \\dim:\\; 6 = 1 + 5 ,</code></pre>\n<p><em>so the traceless part <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Sym}^2(V_1) \\ominus V_0</code> is the single simple object <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_2</code>, of spin <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code> and dimension <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">5</code>.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Proof.</strong> By Clebsch–Gordan <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"fulton-harris1991\">[fulton-harris1991]</span>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_1 \\otimes V_1 \\cong V_0 \\oplus V_1 \\oplus V_2</code>, and the summand <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_k</code> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_j \\otimes V_j</code> lies in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Sym}^2(V_j)</code> exactly when <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k \\equiv 2j \\pmod 2</code>. For <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">j = 1</code> this places <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_0</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_2</code> in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Sym}^2(V_1)</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_1</code> in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Lambda^2(V_1)</code>. The summand <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_0</code> is spanned by the invariant symmetric form on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_1</code>, so removing it leaves <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_2</code>. Its dimension is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2 \\cdot 2 + 1 = 5</code>, the <a href=\"#ex:spin-labels-su2\">spin-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code> entry</a> of the dimension table, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1 + 5 = 6 = \\binom{4}{2}</code>. <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\square</code></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of the proof.</strong> The Clebsch–Gordan decomposition is not proved here. It enters as a definition: the index set of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k \\le 2j</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k \\equiv 2j \\pmod 2</code>. On this index model four facts are proved: the singlet index <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code> occurs for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2j = 2</code>; removing it leaves exactly the index <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code>; that index carries the spin label <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2j = 4</code>; and the dimensions sum to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">6 = 1 + 5</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/sym2-adjoint-traceless-spin-two.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"4.2.11","page":"b/prop-sym2-adjoint-traceless-spin-two","lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.EightfoldWay.Sym2AdjointSpinTwo.adjoint_sym2_traceless_is_spin_two","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/Sym2AdjointSpinTwo.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
